rsx draw engine: a block-compressed (DXT) 3D texture goes up as a volume, its slices out of NVIDIA's VTC order.

Resistance 3's explosion smoke (Chimera rockets, hybrids blowing up) samples 256x256x16 DXT5 volumes in main memory
(SET_TEXTURE_FORMAT 0x0001883A: dimension 3, DXT45; CONTROL3 depth 16), the animation running along the third
coordinate. The pin's 3D path (1ba3657) takes uncompressed formats only, so a DXT volume went up as the 2D image its
first 64 KB make while the fragment program, given the unit in the volume mask, declared it Texture3D. Those 64 KB are
four slices' blocks interleaved, and one of the volumes holds a near-empty first group whose every fourth block is
opaque black: the smoke drew as dark translucent squares with hard edges.

- eng_texture_upload: block-compressed formats take the 3D path too. A level whose width and height are powers of two
  is stored in VTC order (slices in groups of four, the four slices' blocks at one position next to each other, the
  depth % 4 slices left over grouped the same way); eng_unvtc_3d_slice lays a slice out of it into the staging rows,
  written from the NV_texture_compression_vtc spec alone (cited in the source; for the last group, where the
  spec's blockIndex formula and its prose differ, the prose). Any other level is slice after slice.
- Metal texture_upload_3d: a block-compressed slice spans its block rows (bytesPerImage was row bytes x texel rows,
  four times the slice; harmless while each upload is one slice, but not what the call means).

test_rsx_draw_engine: an 8x8x6 DXT5 volume (a group of four and a group of two) goes up as six slices with each block
where its slice put it; a 12x4x2 one goes up slice after slice; a 16x16x8 DXT1 volume with three levels (8, 4 and 2
slices) goes up level by level out of each level's own VTC order. Without the change none reaches texture_upload_3d;
a VTC order without the last group's own stride, none at all, or levels not a whole level apart put blocks in the
wrong slices. Clean under AddressSanitizer. In the game: a pass dump at the squares (Haven street fight) traced them
to the draws of the 0x053B3E00 and 0x051B3E00 volumes; their bytes taken out of VTC order are the smoke's slices.

Upstream: PR #585 (on master the test also turns engine_up into engine_up_with(backend), which a local patch did here).
